{"id": "EUVD-2026-28579", "enisaUuid": "b5b709f4-d310-33af-9cb8-dea22bc83281", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd raid: fix hang when stopping arrays with metadata through dm-raid\n\nWhen using device-mapper's dm-raid target, stopping a RAID array can cause\nthe system to hang under specific conditions.\n\nThis occurs when:\n\n- A dm-raid managed device tree is suspended from top to bottom\n   (the top-level RAID device is suspended first, followed by its\n    underlying metadata and data devices)\n\n- The top-level RAID device is then removed\n\nRemoving the top-level device triggers a hang in the following sequence:\nthe dm-raid destructor calls md_stop(), which tries to flush the\nwrite-intent bitmap by writing to the metadata sub-devices. However, these\ndevices are already suspended, making them unable to complete the write-intent\noperations and causing an indefinite block.\n\nFix:\n\n- Prevent bitmap flushing when md_stop() is called from dm-raid\ndestructor context\n  and avoid a quiescing/unquescing cycle which could also cause I/O\n\n- Still allow write-intent bitmap flushing when called from dm-raid\nsuspend context\n\nThis ensures that RAID array teardown can complete successfully even when the\nunderlying devices are in a suspended state.\n\nThis second patch uses md_is_rdwr() to distinguish between suspend and\ndestructor paths as elaborated on above.", "datePublished": "2026-05-08T13:11:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:40:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/63054027d95200b04f3cf624faa7817e0555d56a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/24783dd06de870d646c25207bae186f78195f912", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/338378dfffbdbb8d37a18f0a0c0358812671f91e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cefcb9297fbdb6d94b61787b4f8d84f55b741470"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v56g-44rc-67wq", "CVE-2026-43309"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "014ead8e-11b1-32e0-972a-a47410e64dac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.19.6 <5.20"}, {"id": "1613d3c6-d0f7-34c4-a9cb-3acbd597929e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}, {"id": "27f06682-9f44-35a8-bce1-08c88b1a8d18", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0dd84b319352bb8ba64752d4e45396d8b13e6018 <cefcb9297fbdb6d94b61787b4f8d84f55b741470"}, {"id": "643d14f1-2f8c-34dd-88ca-ce29b3b65533", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1678ca35b80a94d474fdc31e2497ce5d7ed52512"}, {"id": "6dd32c93-cbd1-394d-916c-ebc1d2d39076", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5a58fab556bfe618b4c9719eb85712d78c6cb10"}, {"id": "722e682b-681e-3881-9b80-0de8fa4fd913", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8e7fb19f1a744fd34e982633ced756fee0498ef7"}, {"id": "741830be-6ed1-38ba-9a5a-451e9af002b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0dd84b319352bb8ba64752d4e45396d8b13e6018 <24783dd06de870d646c25207bae186f78195f912"}, {"id": "77769f85-d9e5-3c8f-818e-78727462e2e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.64 <5.16"}, {"id": "7cfcd491-401e-3085-b727-de9db3c49266", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f42a9819ba84bed2e609a4dff56af37063dcabdc"}, {"id": "a1647753-1d8e-3c84-9f0c-1d128e6b04ad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "661c01b2181d9413c799127f13143583b69f20fd"}, {"id": "a31b49cc-7750-3e1c-ac31-7beffde68f8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a3b5d6e5-eaf2-3b19-a044-333cbdded9e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.6"}, {"id": "a95a9a13-da1d-38e0-abfb-bc941c1ac858", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "b95d902a-cae5-36ea-a13e-4b1f9eb08b0f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.14.292 <4.15"}, {"id": "bb4e6269-21cc-3ce6-ba4d-780c807d1d35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.140 <5.11"}, {"id": "c40f7ae7-6d58-342a-be9a-73835a490fe2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0dd84b319352bb8ba64752d4e45396d8b13e6018 <338378dfffbdbb8d37a18f0a0c0358812671f91e"}, {"id": "c53bfa1a-67ed-3d38-bf2b-4eca393cd807", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.19.257 <4.20"}, {"id": "ccab9707-9e3b-3134-ade1-c2035f876b98", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "d5dff615-c4cd-374a-865d-e6b6e5e8074d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "690b5c90fd2d81fd1d2b6110fa36783232f6dce2"}, {"id": "dc6c061c-410f-30b6-8315-d4856a302584", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0dd84b319352bb8ba64752d4e45396d8b13e6018 <63054027d95200b04f3cf624faa7817e0555d56a"}, {"id": "e80cc7fb-2d83-3736-b183-aabb161c219f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.4.212 <5.5"}, {"id": "fe7fd14d-ef83-3bba-a411-67da87f5e269", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.16"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e4ac9e5f-4577-34e0-813f-541e774d6527", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}